red_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"GwfFkFb7RDbq4qHD_CUuIA","review_id":"Kcsps2uHTt8zc38joKvDtg","date":"2006-12-19T19:51:19","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9426270723342896,"text_excerpt":"this is one of those places that's the heart and soul of new orleans. It used to be a churches chicken, like 40 years ago, and you can verify that by reading the labels on the really old fryers just behind the very old bulletproof glass that separated the order counter from the kitchen. Don;t be alarmed. In Nola baby, if a dive looks scary enough that you think twice about eating there... you TOTALLY need to. The angry looking vietnamese fellow is Mr. Lee, and he and his wife will amaze you with their high high taste and low low prices. Best bets: (like sammy said) the BBQ pork poboy, which they pull off ribs (that you can get on a platter by themselves or as chinese food), the 2-for- 1.7..."},{"business_id":"GwfFkFb7RDbq4qHD_CUuIA","review_id":"d0N9O8VKTqcbHNmTDhYeHg","date":"2008-10-13T18:59:37","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9373416304588318,"text_excerpt":"I used to go to the Valence Church across the street. This place closes by 7:30pm so go early. However bad it looks from the outside this is one of my favorite take-outs (the only way you can eat here-no tables). I have tried the po-boys-great bread-the chinese food, the fried fish, it's ALL very good and cheap. Only in New Orleans baby!"},{"business_id":"GwfFkFb7RDbq4qHD_CUuIA","review_id":"fySCWQf4Q_Q3-QH7MeZo0Q","date":"2014-09-11T17:16:42","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.8982780575752258,"text_excerpt":"Delicious shrimp po' boys. Can't wait to try the bun and chicken. I am just a shrimp po' boy lover so it is hard for me to pull myself away."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
